From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: computerguy526 <355510486+computerguy526@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:49:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: gpusafe: fail-safe environment values, device
 teardown, uptime clock, clamp after predication

- Environment numbers go through kk_safe_parse_num: a value that is not a
  plain number inside its range keeps the default and is reported. Before,
  atof() turned a typo into 0, which switched the guard off, and an
  out-of-range value reached an integer conversion.
- kk_safe_device_destroy: the clamp counter and the loop-state chunks live in
  one device's residency set. They are released with that device and the next
  device gets its own; a second live device is refused the state instead of
  being handed addresses that are not resident for it. The device pointer used
  by the OOM dump is cleared.
- The watchdog measures awake time (CLOCK_UPTIME_RAW): a commit in flight when
  the machine sleeps is not overdue on wake.
- Indirect dispatches predicated by conditional rendering are clamped too; the
  direct and indirect paths log their first suppression independently.
- The GPU-free tests of kk_safety_core.h live in vulkan/tests and are
  registered with meson (suite kosmickrisp).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
